+# Reading basis and exact continuation
+
+The GitHub default branch read was `20709bee872ad10e4cc7d7b976d975e24532a803`.
+It confirms the integrated mixed-fibre/middle-spectrum work. It did not confirm
+the latest square-zero/Pell tranche. The available incoming directory and branch
+list were checked; this is not a statement that the work exists nowhere else.
+
+The supplied square-zero source was read in full through Files, with its handoff.
+Its SHA-256 is `f3a3a87cde84c1bad100f56dc422d9d2bc49a7c18924da48377ac8670ea9e453`.
+The supplied archive SHA-256 is `2697ddb6ada7e088ec172eed495f4e215d6b088b57fd707a2170960fdf0a91ff`.
+The attached ten-stage plan was read and continues to place universal original
+occupancy, not another receiver norm, at the missing Stage7 step.
+
+Inherited and retained: original E/M normalization and ordered denominators;
+trace square gates; K,D and the square-zero fine defect; the complete original
+box partition; its integer coefficients and stabilizers; the unit-width
+criterion; factor-sum/Pell map; and the p67369 nonincreasing-repair obstruction.
+The upstream orientation, carrier, and integer-versus-vector-section corrections
+remain in force. No extra orientation bit is added to an already ordered M word.
+
+Added here: the bounded mixed-order cyclic section and explicit carried law;
+its exact multiplicity lower bound and optimal divisor-DAG criterion; actual
+hard-prime realizations beyond the unit-width criterion; arithmetic sharpness at
+an arbitrary odd defect; and a plus-factor relation crossing the critical trace
+upwards by one shell, with an infinite reduced prime family and full inverse
+fibres. These are not consequences of receiver invertibility.
+
+The new complete original census is p=1 mod24 through10000. It does not reuse the
+predecessor's execution count, and the new p67369 prefix check is not described
+as an independent reproof of leastness over all817 earlier primes. Isolated
+large primes have complete-order certificates separate from discovery.
+
+One exploratory factor-neighbour graph was considered but is not used as a
+closure theorem. The delivered fixed-C negative control proves that even all
+original gates in a plus-factor fibre may be empty. No speculative global graph
+connectivity or termination assertion is imported.
